 "brief": "A tool adapter between my arm's wrist flange and a small gripper, printed in Ti64 on a metal\npowder-bed machine, built along +Z. Wrist side: a 40 mm diameter, 4 mm thick disc at z = 0 to 4\nwith four M4 clearance holes (4.5 mm) on a 31.5 mm circle at 45, 135, 225 and 315 degrees;\nthe wrist holds it there. Tool side: a 30 x 30 mm, 3 mm thick plate at z = 37 to 40 with four\nM3 clearance holes (3.4 mm) on a 25 mm square; the gripper bolts onto its top face. A 12 mm air\nhose runs straight through the middle along Z, keep that clear. Everything within a 22 mm\nradius of the Z axis, z = 0 to 40. The gripper is 0.4 kg with its centre of mass 80 mm above\nthe tool plate, and in a crash it can see 5 g sideways. Safety factor 3, under 45 g.",
